1. Download the files:
   WSLInstall.ps1
   WSLQuickSetup.sh (for a quicker setup)
   WSLFullSetup.sh (for more tools installed)
2. Open PowerShell as administrator
3. Run:
   Unblock-File -Path "PATH TO YOUR FILE"
      EG: C:\Users\Name\Downloads\WSLInstall.ps1
4. Open the file
5. Run:
   .\WSLInstall.ps1
6. Once it finishes, restart your computer
7. Wait for the WSL setup to launch, then when prompted, provide your desired username and password 
8. Once set up, simply run "WSL" in your compand prompt or in your file explorer to launch your Ubuntu

Note: if steps 7 and 8 did not work, try running the script again, Ubuntu may not have installed the first time

9. For a quick setup, follow these instructions:
1. Move the WSLQuickSetup.sh file into your WSL user directory (The directory will show up at the bottom of your file explorer)
2. Run:
   sudo chmod +x WSLQuickSetup.sh
3. Run:
   sudo ./WSLQuickSetup.sh
4. Enter Your Password
(You may be required to hit enter a few times during the setup process)
5. Once complete, close your terminal and open a new one and everything should be set up

10. For a full setup, follow these instructions:
1. Move the WSLFullSetup.sh file into your WSL user directory (The directory will show up at the bottom of your file explorer)
2. Run:
      sudo chmod +x WSLFullSetup.sh
3. Run:
   sudo ./WSLFullSetup.sh
4. Enter Your Password
(You may be required to hit enter a few times during the setup process.)
5. Once complete, close your terminal and open a new one and everything should be set up


Extra Notes:
To start your python virtual environment in order to be able to use pip install, use:
   source .venv/bin/activate
To close your virtual environment, Use:
   deactivate
